0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 745 Td (NAT rewrites IP addresses at a network boundary. Static NAT maps one inside-local address to) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 730 Td (one inside-global address; dynamic NAT allocates from a pool; PAT \(NAT overload\) maps many) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 715 Td (inside hosts to one global address using transport ports. Terms include inside local, inside) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 700 Td (global, outside local, and outside global. NAT conserves IPv4 addresses but adds state and) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 685 Td (can complicate inbound connections.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg BT /F2 12 Tf 55 664 Td (Operating principles) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 643 Td (Network Address Translation \(NAT\) can be understood by following a communication from its) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 628 Td (source through the relevant interfaces and protocol layers. Each device processes only the) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 613 Td (information needed for its role. Correct operation depends on consistent addressing,) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 598 Td (compatible link settings, correct service configuration, and a return path for replies.) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 577 Td (At the link layer, frames carry local delivery information such as source and destination) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 562 Td (MAC addresses. At the network layer, IP addresses and routing decisions identify the path) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 547 Td (between subnets. Transport and application protocols provide the end-to-end service when) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 532 Td (required. A failure at any layer can prevent the expected application behavior.) Tj ET
0 0 0 rg BT /F2 12 Tf 55 511 Td (Important terms) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 490 Td (Key terms for this lab include network address translation \(nat\), interface state,) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 475 Td (addressing, forwarding, and verification. Distinguish configuration state from observed) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 460 Td (behavior: a command being accepted does not by itself prove that end-to-end communication) Tj ET
0.08 0.08 0.08 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 55 445 Td (works.) Tj ET
